## Specification diagnostics

A linear model assumes a constant rate of association across the data range and errors that are symmetric and evenly spread around the fit. We test those assumptions with three diagnostics, the residuals plotted against fitted values, a QQ plot of the residuals, and the variance inflation factors already reported. @fig-resid-analysis shows the first two, and both point to the same failure. The smoothed residual line departs from zero, which indicates curvature the model does not capture, and the vertical spread of residuals widens with fitted values. The model underestimates both the lowest and the highest purchasing power counties while fitting the middle well. The QQ plot departs from normality in the upper tail, reflecting a residual skew of 1.01.
:::

::: {#4f672bed .cell .hidden execution_count=11}
``` {.python .cell-code .hidden}
resid_df=reg[["fitted","resid"]].copy()
smooth_level=lowess(reg["resid"], reg["fitted"], return_sorted=True)
smooth_level_df=pd.DataFrame(smooth_level, columns=["fitted","resid"])
```
:::


::: {#cell-fig-resid-analysis .cell execution_count=12}
