:::{#8b3ece12 .cell .markdown}
### Collinearity

The four task groups are parts of a whole, so one must be removed, since the fourth is determined once the other three are known. Leaving all four in would guarantee at least one variance inflation offender, for the reason set out in @fig-vif. The remaining three coefficients read as the change in purchasing power associated with a shift toward that group and away from the omitted one.
:::

::: {#cd4608e6 .cell .hidden execution_count=26}
``` {.python .cell-code .hidden}
exposure_check_cols=["routine_cognitive_share",
    "routine_manual_share",
    "non_routine_cognitive_share",
    "non_routine_manual_share"]

REFERENCE_EXPOSURE="non_routine_cognitive_share"
exposure_cols_model=[c for c in exposure_check_cols if c!=REFERENCE_EXPOSURE]
core_features=exposure_cols_model+["poverty_rate", "unemployment_rate"]
```
:::


::: {#tbl-vif-ml .cell tbl-cap='Ten highest variance inflation factors among year and state indicators after removing the reference task group. All values fall below 5, indicating no remaining collinearity concern.' execution_count=27}
